<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine weekly official crop progress.</title>
<headline>Argentine weekly official crop progress.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The most advanced wheat Argentina's Buenos Aires province were beginning to form ears Oct 18, Agriculture Secretariat said Thursday in its weekly crop report.</p>
<p>The most advanced wheat in Santa Fe Cordoba, and Entre Rios are beginning to form grains. Sunny days would be welcome in Buenos Aires and La Pampa to ward off the threat of fungus. But the sanitary condition of most wheat is optimum. Some 70.2 poercent of wheat was fertilized in Buenos Aires province, but only 30.3 percent in La Pampa. Some 72 percent more hectares of wheat were fertilized this season than in 1995/96.  </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets). Yield in quintals per hectare.</p>
<p> ..........Planting.............Harvest..................Yield</p>
